## Standalone review (on demand only)

Run this only in **standalone review mode**. **Read-only:** do not edit code, commit, push, post PR comments, approve, or check out branches.

Use **`AskQuestion`** for every gate below. If the tool is unavailable, ask the same options in chat and wait.

### 1. Scope (single-select)

| Option | Scope |
|---|---|
| **Ticket local changes** | Commits on the current branch that are not on the base branch, plus uncommitted work (staged, unstaged, and untracked task files) |
| **PR review** | A GitHub PR the user names (number or URL) |
| **Other** | The user describes the scope in chat (paths, commit range, branch compare) |

### 2. Resolve scope

- **Ticket local changes:**
  - **AskQuestion** to confirm the base branch. Default: the branch upstream base, else the repo default branch (`git symbolic-ref refs/remotes/origin/HEAD`).
  - Diff: `git log <base>..HEAD --oneline`, `git diff <base>...HEAD`, plus `git diff`, `git diff --staged`, and `git status --short`.
  - Ticket key from the branch name (`[A-Z]+-\d+`). If missing, ask, or use `no-ticket`.
- **PR review:**
  - If the PR is not given, ask for it.
  - Read with `gh pr view <n> --json number,title,baseRefName,headRefName,files,body` and `gh pr diff <n>`.
  - Show title, base, head, and file count before reviewing.
- **Other:** restate the resolved scope and **AskQuestion** to confirm before reviewing.
- **Large scope** (more than about 30 changed files): **AskQuestion** — narrow scope / proceed / cancel.

### 3. Review

Review the diff against this rule: design, scope, reuse, overfitting, over-engineering, readability, errors and fallbacks, performance, tests, and AI concerns when relevant. Apply [Python layout](#python-layout) only to `.py` files. Point to files and lines. Give each finding one home (Blocking, Follow-ups, or Residual risks).

### 4. Report (always)

Always write a report, even when the review looks good. Follow [`y-agt-workspace`](../agent/y-agt-workspace.mdc).

- **Path:** `cursor_workspace/engineering-review/engineering-review-<jira-key>-<YYYYMMDD-HHMM>-<scope-slug>.md`
  - All lowercase. `mkdir -p` first. Do not overwrite earlier reports.
  - `jira-key`: lowercase key (for example `vap-3547`), or `no-ticket`.
  - `YYYYMMDD-HHMM`: 24-hour local time when the report is written.
  - `scope-slug`: branch slug for ticket local changes, `pr-<number>` for a PR, a short kebab slug for other scopes.
- **H1:** `Engineering Review - <JIRA> - <YYYYMMDD-HHMM> - <scope-slug>`. Normal Jira casing is fine in the H1. Timestamp and slug must match the filename.

```markdown
# Engineering Review - VAP-3547 - 20261006-2130 - feature-vap-3547-explain-insight

**Scope type:** Ticket local changes | PR review | Other
**Branch / PR:** …
**Base:** …
**Verdict:** Approve | Approve with follow-ups | Request changes

## Scores
(six metrics per Review scores)

## Scope
(commits, PR, or paths reviewed; file count)

## What works well
(only if useful)

## Blocking
(numbered; must fix before merge)

## Follow-ups
(numbered; non-blocking)

## Residual risks
(bullets)
```

Omit empty sections except **Scores** and **Scope**. B2 English. No secrets.

### 5. Chat summary

Verdict, scores, the top blocking items (if any), and the report path.

